WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.437
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.401 --> 00:00:07.040
SPEAKER: Give me
one minute, and I'll

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.160
show you how Cloud Run can
help you create apps quickly.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:12.560
Cloud Run is a fully
managed compute environment

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:15.290
that lets you easily deploy
stateless containers.

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:17.270
It abstracts away
infrastructure management

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:19.700
and scales up and down
with your app's traffic,

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.350
and you only pay when
your code is running.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:23.960
Cloud Run is easy to use.

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:26.780
Just write your app using your
favorite language, framework,

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:30.020
and/or binary libraries,
package the app as a container,

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:32.720
and deploy it using
gcloud run deploy.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:35.450
And just like that,
your app is live.

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:38.350
By default, your service
gets an HTTPS endpoint

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:41.060
with TLS termination
on your custom domain.

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:43.640
And since Cloud Run is built
on the native open standard,

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:45.200
you can easily move
your applications

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:48.650
to any Kubernetes
clusters-- on GCP, on-prem,

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:50.600
or in another cloud.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:53.220
Using Cloud Run, you can build
client-driven web services,

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:55.100
such as dynamic
websites, mobile app

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:57.885
back ends, or back
office administration.

00:00:57.885 --> 00:00:59.510
You can also use
Cloud Run for creating

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:01.920
automated, asynchronous
microservices,

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:03.740
such as lightweight
data transformation,

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:06.260
scheduled document generation,
or business workflow

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:07.120
automation.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:09.120
Next time you're thinking
about building an app,

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:10.910
take a minute to
look at Cloud Run.

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:14.530
To learn more, check out
cloud.google.com/run.

